{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual","id":1368060,"title":"Hi, is this game 100% straight and fully heterosexual?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-15T10:20:28-08:00","id":1368060,"title":"Hi, is this game 100% straight and fully heterosexual?","content":"<img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/498704231407288320/678252517498290186/VS.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <hr /><br /> So in my previous <span style=\"color:#EE82EE\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">The Gay</span></span> vs <span style=\"color:#008000\">Cthulhu </span>thread, some of the points raised have made me ponder about something.<br /> <br /> The premise when I made that thread is people should stop thinking about sexual orientation when using Celestial Bliss Trick since the people that you are going to seduce are not gay people, it's giant talking tornado, the transdimensional center of the observable universe, Sauron's armor, and Cthulhu obviously...etc, they don't have the human concept of sexuality or genders.<br /> <br /> But when I look at Exalted, I have to wonder if they do indeed possess such traits in Creation? Since many canon non-human NPCs are clearly written with obvious gender and sexuality traits that are very similar to human, from obvious things like male demons such as Florivet being described as a womanizer or the Ebon Dragon marrying a woman, to subtle things like most romantic and sexual text concerning non-human are usually between the opposite sex, take the Sun for example, no books ever mention anything about male NPCs having feeling for him, but it does for the Maiden, Luna, or Merela (and that chariot goddess in Glories: UCS iirc). So my question is whether most non-human in Exalted possesses the same sexual orientation and gender identities as humans?<br /> <br /> Another question that I'm thinking about that also appear in the Cthulhu thread is <i>The Gay Bard</i>. So basically gay people are a minority of the population, if we assume that this is also true in Exalted, and the answer to the above question about non-human is Yes, then would gay seducers constantly barking at the wrong tree since 80% of everything is straight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T10:40:45-08:00","id":1368064,"title":"","content":"Huh. I don't think I've ever thought about this before.<br /> <br /> I believe that books such as Roll of Glorious Divinity describe a state in which romantic or sexual relationships between spirits wouldn't have the trends that humans have when talking broadly in the abstract, but it does seem that in practice hetero bias predominates significantly when there are any actual specific descriptions of them. Off hand I can remember two gods described as being in same-sex relationships with other gods, Wun Ja of the Shining Metropolis and Jagalza Satrap of the Realm (can't recall if it was with each other).<br /> <br /> And then there's Luna and Gaia, a subject I was introduced to in terms of them both being female entities, and I'd say still counts with the former being genderfluid. The illustration in Games of Divinity shows Gaia sitting alongside a masculine Luna, and while not inaccurate even then it kind of makes me wonder if it doesn't reinforce heteronormativity.<br /> <br /> I think there's... a Sidereal guy who has a relationship with a male-coded god? Off the top of my head, I can't recall concrete descriptions of queer relationships between gods and humans.<br /> <br /> And it's rather a missed opportunity, since there's a lot of capacity to use that side of gods to represent and explore matters of gender and sexual relationships to beings with no reproductive drives, or even necessity to stick to conventions (there's description of the potential for masculine gods to bear children).<br /> <br /> Yeah, this was a good thing to bring attention to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T10:52:43-08:00","id":1368066,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded that the bit about Holden intending Dreadful Adjudicator of Law to be gender fluid in his Scroll of Exalts backstory and that getting changed to a heteronormative relationship in editing, I refuse to believe that it was the only time in the history of this gameline that an editor either chickened out or assumed pronouns were being used in error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T11:38:10-08:00","id":1368080,"title":"","content":"this is an interesting question because I think that, from what I've seen, actual games are often far more gay then the game's description. The game line itself often seems to suggest or want to present non cishet relationships; I think it was actively a design goal in 3E as well, but it can sometimes seem to fall flat. Lioness has also done a lot of work in cataloguing things like how the Realm isn't really a Matriarchy in prior editions, and I think it speaks to the idea that the Gameline often said these things, and didn't always do the legwork in presenting it, but the players often seem willing to grab onto those sayings and do the legwork themselves in presenting them.<br /> <br /> But then when you get into the spirits and gods of Exalted, I also think you're correct. They aren't often generally presented as alien or non-human, and instead just human people who are sometimes a little weird looking. It's more then just their relationships and presentation, though I think you're right that it's part of it in the same way the rest of the gameline kind of revolves around it doing a lot of telling and not being strong enough to show.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I think the idea of Gods being human like, with flaws, idiosyncacies that are innately human, etc, is also sometimes strong and a good part of them existing. Assigning all gods to a kind of blue and orange morality just because it spices it up could also be considered a bit awkward in my opinion, because it severely limits what you can do with them unless you're quite competent.<br /> <br /> For instance, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1115_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1115\" data-vbnamecard=\"1115\">The Hug Ninja</a> portrays her Gods as being incredibly difficult to understand; a common theme is having to possess people in order to even talk to others because actually showing up could cause colossal damage and upheaval. She's done this for the gods of a character's culture and for the Elemental Dragon that rules Champoor. This is, I think, because she's a big fan of Conan and Eldric, where similar things occurred with their Gods. This makes them seem very distant and non-human, but it also does mean there's limited interaction with them as a whole. It's interesting, but a delicate balancing act that she has to carry out- from how I see it-, to maintain interest in something that your interaction with is intensely limited.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar535_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"535\" data-vbnamecard=\"535\">Bastet</a> 's Sidereal game does more work presenting Gods as being very human in their interactions. They look weird or strange and sometimes they have a lot better memory then you do, but in the end they still are kind of working towards similar goals; they want money or power or to better the world, and interacting with them on that axis is generally the most favorable way to get them to help you.<br /> <br /> The presentations are very different but it's because they're aiming for two different tonal stories that the Gods and Elementals are manipulated to present those different stories in an effective way.<br /> <br /> So I don't know if Gods and Demons and Elementals should always be completely alien and difficult to understand, but I don't know if it should be impossible for them to be that either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 02-15-2020, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T12:04:46-08:00","id":1368085,"title":"","content":"I can remember a conversation back when Holden was about, when we discussed if the Incarna and Primordials *really* had genders, and HLS was pretty ardently of the opinion that they should have, because the audience essentially did, and would want to see themselves largely as represented as mirrors reality, and this was a big point in being able empathize with them as characters, and they wouldn't empathize with them if they were at a high frequently gender neutral (or intersex or transgender, although he didn't actually say that bit). Hopefully I'm not mangling his opinion here, as this is an old conversation and I can't even give a link.<br /> <br /> (My stance, as I remember it, as one of the folks in that thread was a bit more, to paraphrase, like &quot;Obviously human sexes and genders are just a kind of legacy of us being sexually reproducing animals and it's dumb and limiting to sort of propose that these states are hard coded into existence as a fundamental spiritual property of reality, and to boot kind of normalizes sex and gender essentialism in our world and politics in ways that I don't like involving them having a spiritual dimension. Give me my post-gender gods who aren't men or women, please. So much more interesting than getting hung up on these kind of boring legacy states of human being from our reality.&quot; I don't know if I'd take that stance today, or not, or be more sympathetic to other stances!)<br /> <br /> I figure on the same basis if you're probably going to extend the notion of divine beings having romantic drives, you're probably going to do so on the basis that again mirrors what gives most of the audience that same sense of connection to themselves and their own relationships, or it would be kind of inconsistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T12:32:29-08:00","id":1368095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368080#post1368080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is an interesting question because I think that, from what I've seen, actual games are often far more gay then the game's description. The game line itself often seems to suggest or want to present non cishet relationships; I think it was actively a design goal in 3E as well, but it can sometimes seem to fall flat. Lioness has also done a lot of work in cataloguing things like how the Realm isn't really a Matriarchy in prior editions, and I think it speaks to the idea that the Gameline often said these things, and didn't always do the legwork in presenting it, but the players often seem willing to grab onto those sayings and do the legwork themselves in presenting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second edition actually tried to offer an explaination why there were so many gay and bisexual Dragon-Blooded. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Dragon-Blooded page 50</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the entire first year of their existence, the lives of those who composed the Dragon-Blooded Host were more akin to never-ending orgies than anything resembling warfare. Solar generals found themselves fitting combat training in between the Terrestrials\u2019 extended bouts of rutting. Once all of the female Terrestrials were impregnated and well along in their pregnancies, however, the situation changed drastically. Mortal women might have been forbidden to the lusty Dragon-Blooded men but everyone (and everything) else was fair game, and historians claim that the frequency of homosexual relations among the Dragon-Blooded dates back to this period.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wish they hadn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T14:19:43-08:00","id":1368129,"title":"","content":"3E does seem to be trying to normalize non-heteronormativity. Sometimes it's in little things like the core mentioning an Inspire action reminding a deathknight of his late husband, sometimes it's more overt like the DB text addressing homosexual and trans identities (the former especially in acknowledging same-sex Dynastic marriages as opposed to just same-sex extramarital affairs), or Lunars having multiple canon trans characters and Luna themselves having neutral pronouns by default.<br /> <br /> Also, Lioness, that passage gets an entire yike from me. I continue to be glad that WFHW was the first DB-related thing I paid much attention to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:10:40-08:00","id":1368144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual#post1368060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my question is whether most non-human in Exalted possesses the same sexual orientation and gender identities as humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that <i>many</i> such creatures do so, yes, even if I wouldn't necessarily commit to saying &quot;most&quot;. There's a couple reasons for that. In-setting, it seems like there's something metaphysically significant about a humanoid form. There are a lot of creatures that, despite not being humans, still <i>look</i> like humans, and they don't all post-date humanity's ascension to prominence, either. Many demons seem to have had basically humanoid forms before the War of the Gods, for example, and several primordial races (the Lintha, for example, and the weird alien Grey-style race that Autochthon ate) seem to have been humanoid, but produced before or at least simultaneously to humans. And having genders, with the spectrum with two main &quot;poles&quot; like humans do, seems to be quite common as well - the Dragon Kings have it, for instance. So, in short, in-setting, a roughly human-like gender distribution is possibly not just an accident of one species, but has some kind of cosmological significance.<br /> <br /> The other reason, the out-of-game one, for many non-human creatures to nevertheless have something approaching human gender, sexual identity, and desire is that it gives human characters more opportunities to interact with them. If you can't seduce a god because they don't have a gender identity and would be equally likely to be sexually attracted by a shade of blue, that cuts off an avenue for some characters. Suddenly, the seducer character can't really participate in the scene, even in terms of suggesting to someone else what might make <i>them</i> attractive. The more those opportunities are reduced, the more the players will tend to default to &quot;just punch it&quot;. And that's an outcome I prefer to avoid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically gay people are a minority of the population, if we assume that this is also true in Exalted, and the answer to the above question about non-human is Yes, then would gay seducers constantly barking at the wrong tree since 80% of everything is straight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the answer here is two-fold. First, I'd straight-up (pun not intended!) make homosexual, asexual, and other non-hetero orientations more common in Creation. Like, maybe 30% of humans, at least, are a full 6 on the Kinsey Scale? Second, I would say that the <i>stigmatization</i> of non-heterosexuality is much, much less common in Creation than it is on Earth. As a result, far more people who aren't full 6s on the Kinsey Scale, but who aren't full 0s either (that is, not exclusively <i>hetero</i>-sexually attracted) are willing to act on those desires. I believe research on Earth on real humans has suggested that the majority are <i>some</i> degree of bisexual, rather than having exclusive heterosexual desire, so this would essentially just be treating humans more &quot;realistically&quot; anyway. And fully homosexual people will also be more willing to openly announce that fact, presenting more opportunities for the gay seducer who wanted to focus on exclusively homosexual people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T15:43:00-08:00","id":1368155,"title":"","content":"I can't say anything to developer intention or setting lore, but I explained to my players like this: In Creation, everyone is presumed Bi unless otherwise clarified- there are 100% straight and 100% gay and 100% Ace people, but generally speaking, the way you assume an IRL person is straight unless otherwise mentioned is the way Creation assumes people are bi. Each person is somewhere on the Kinsey scale and nobody gives a damn about who you like. <br /> <br /> I run gods and spirits as being ... alien, kind of. The River Mother favors women since she believes herself to be tied to the concept of motherhood, but she also loves men as potential fathers. Alasathasas the Tears of the Mountain is a god of song- &quot;he&quot; doesn't care about male/female, he's only attracted to how musically gifted someone is. One creepy god of kelp, drowning, and Wu-Jian's wells is attracted to how beautiful your neck is and how much pleasure she'd get out of drowning you with her hands around it. <br /> <br /> To say one thing about the Realm though, I told my players that there's a lot of unofficial support specifically for homosexuality, because marriages are arranged on dynastic terms and you <b>will</b> pop out babies, whether you like your spouse or not. Since its expected that Dynasts will have affairs and trysts as long as they are discreet and kept out of public view, its a huge boon to take a same-sex lover because there's no risk of surprise pregnancy (Which I don't need to tell would be a huge political shit show amongst the houses). <br /> <br /> So basically, it never comes up unless I decide that a certain character has a specific kink. My 2e Giant Athletics Night Caste Batman was gay, and <i>only</i> for huge muscle dudes. A standard sexy-kimono-courtesan tried to charm him and she was treated like a whiny child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T17:22:13-08:00","id":1368177,"title":"","content":"The Lintha looked human because they were human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368129#post1368129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3E does seem to be trying to normalize non-heteronormativity.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was always like that, really. I find it makes a blind spot with regards to how gods relate to one another and to humans stand out to me more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T23:18:37-08:00","id":1368229,"title":"","content":"Well, I cannot say for everyone else, but lessee, in games I've either STed, or been a player in....<br /> <br /> <b>Don Flamenco</b>, a Joybringer who stylized himself a warrior of love in all its forms. Think bosozoku Freddie Mercury, and you wouldn't be too far off. (In)famous for his Flamenco Vision, which could offer him all sorts of naughty secrets.<br /> <br /> <b>Valentinian XIII Callistus</b>, a constantly reborn Solar who swore an oath to eternally serve the UCS, which resulted in his mind following his exaltation, resuming where he last left off, regardless of his host's body. This resulted in my not even knowing his biological sex for three sessions, and when prompted, I tossed a coin, as Valentinian was behind heavy armor before. This resulted in my circle deciding that the gruff, cantankerous knight was, in fact, a teen girl from An-Teng, which was all the more hilarious as I played him like a knight-errant, wooing ladies with courtly love and gallantry. Needless to say, there were many young ladies aflutter with this knight's derring-do.<br /> <br /> <b>Kharas Schneider,</b> a Changing Moon Lothario of the River Province, who sought to make his own kingdom. Deciding the most efficacious way to do so is to make his subjects himself, the old-fashioned way, he has since spent the last three sessions as a woman, seeking a proper sugar daddy.<br /> <br /> <b>Scarlet Wind</b>, a beautiful Solar pirate queen from the Caul whose ravenous lust for the fairer sex actually caused the Byronic fall and ultimate death, of another Solar. Such was her tastes, she sought out rare and exotic cargoes to use as gifts for her female paramours awaiting her return from sea.<br /> <br /> <b>Zebran the Sun Jester</b>, a Solar wandering ascetic who formed his own messianic cult around newly made warrior communities. To distract from this, he made sport of seducing the Wyld Hunts to his side, many times quite literally. He was famous as 'Zebran of the Sun-Spear,' and not for the massive lance he wielded in battle.<br /> <br /> Nope, this is totally on the straight and narrow, my dudes.<br /> <br /> Sarcasm aside, who cares what the 'canon' NPCs are or do in terms of their sexuality or orientation? Isn't the beauty of tabletop games to adjust the fluff or rules as your groups' tastes deem appropriate? If it's what your table wants? Go for it, it's your game, after all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T03:54:37-08:00","id":1368278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368066#post1368066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reminded that the bit about Holden intending Dreadful Adjudicator of Law to be gender fluid in his Scroll of Exalts backstory and that getting changed to a heteronormative relationship in editing, I refuse to believe that it was the only time in the history of this gameline that an editor either chickened out or assumed pronouns were being used in error.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, there is this male 2CD in Game of Divinity who falls in love with a mortal guy who the demon just murdered, and the spirit book in Ex2 tried ridiculously hard not to mention the mortal's gender by repeatedly written their name instead of using he/him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368229#post1368229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sarcasm aside, who cares what the 'canon' NPCs are or do in terms of their sexuality or orientation? Isn't the beauty of tabletop games to adjust the fluff or rules as your groups' tastes deem appropriate? If it's what your table wants? Go for it, it's your game, after all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm, because representation matters??? Are you saying that you don't care about minorities being featured in canon since people can always write fanfic about it instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T04:37:26-08:00","id":1368280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368155#post1368155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">marriages are arranged on dynastic terms and you <b>will</b> pop out babies, whether you like your spouse or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's beneficial how What Fire Has Wrought reconciled this element with love marriages including same-sex relationships by making a point of how the Houses see some use in childless couples as people that can readily take on adoptees.<br /> <br /> That and, if they're willing to take on the stigma, the uses of neomah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T05:55:26-08:00","id":1368290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368280#post1368280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's beneficial how What Fire Has Wrought reconciled this element with love marriages including same-sex relationships by making a point of how the Houses see some use in childless couples as people that can readily take on adoptees.<br /> <br /> That and, if they're willing to take on the stigma, the uses of neomah.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I especially like how the book outright states that if the lovebirds involved are going to go to the effort of actually arguing for their match, their families and Houses recognize it's probably better to have a married and satisfied scion who will probably produce heirs one way or another, as opposed to risking pushing a valuable scion away and getting nothing because they ran off or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T11:29:26-08:00","id":1368337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368278#post1368278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yes, there is this male 2CD in Game of Divinity who falls in love with a mortal guy who the demon just murdered, and the spirit book in Ex2 tried ridiculously hard not to mention the mortal's gender by repeatedly written their name instead of using he/him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's too bad, gay relashionships between gods and mortals were a thing in mythology*. (And in the books of the Flat Earth which are an aknowledged inspiration for Exalted)<br /> <br /> *I remember clearly Apollo &amp; Hyacinth, for example","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>Inevitable Meerkat Style</b></i><br /> <i>The Student Sutra of Spotlight Hoging: Once, there was a maiden, but who cares about those? Let's talk about Lunars.</i>","edited":{"userid":8863,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8863-slulura","user":"Slulura","date":". 02-16-2020, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8863-slulura","name":"Slulura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T11:53:38-08:00","id":1368342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slulura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368337#post1368337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's too bad, gay relashionships between gods and mortals were a thing in mythology*. (And in the books of the Flat Earth which are an aknowledged inspiration for Exalted)<br /> <br /> *I remember clearly Apollo &amp; Hyacinth, for example</div> </div> </div> </div>I think diverse pantheons of multiple cultures have a tendency to represent that culture's awareness of a broad array of human types, real or imagined. I just recently learned of a myth concerning Set and Horus engaged in a contest of collecting one another's semen.<br /> <br /> They've not always carried the most accepting attitudes, but it's a foundation that can be reworked to serve the purposes of this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T12:40:23-08:00","id":1368358,"title":"","content":"There's also a myth where Horus lets Set ejaculate inside him... but this gives Horus power over him, as he's stolen his semen, allowing Horus to defeat Set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:34:14-08:00","id":1368591,"title":"","content":"Many gods, demons, fae, etc. can exhibit the full diversity of sexual orientations and gender identities that humans also have. A lot of the time, we try to write these nonhuman entities as being &quot;people&quot; first and foremost, and having them partake of some of the human condition is often helpful in doing so.<br /> <br /> There probably are orientations and gender identities that some non-humans have that humans don't\u2014in fact, I've got some specific ideas in that regard for the Mountain Folk\u2014but it's hard to find a good place to discuss that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T10:30:45-08:00","id":1369860,"title":"","content":"There's a character I've made and still waiting for a chance to play, Marjan, who's a Dawn Caste, and, more relevant, a daughter and priestess of the (male) god of sparring/martial training.<br /> She was otherwise raised by a (single) mortal man.<br /> I've tried to make the circumstances of her birth sound properly mythological; her parents had no actual romantic or sexual interest in each other, her human father just prayed to the god for combat training in order to prepare for future bandit raids on the village (one could go for more straightforward, easier worship of gods of battles/victory, but those tends to be very in demand by everyone and not necessarily available or willing to answer, and sparring/training offers the added bonus of personal growth). In response, the god manifested directly, and started a very long and intensive training session that his worshiper nonetheless managed to power through; this session was so intense and filled with passion that its conclusion resulted in the manifestation of a newborn human girl, who, besides a knack for varied forms of combat as she grew up and the circumstances of her birth, was completely normal.<br /> <br /> This is the objective, serious pitch.<br /> <br /> But after reading this thread, I can't help but ruin the mythical feel by picturing the scene went more like this:<br /> Man: &quot;Thank you so much, o divine Karoka, I have grown immensely as an individual and protector of my community thanks to you and will be able to teach my peers how to-- wait, is that a baby?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;No need to thank me, that's my domain! And yes, that's our baby.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;Our baby? Ours?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Congratulations! You are the worthy co-progenitor of my spawn! Phew, I haven't had such a great sparring session in a while.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;But... but. We didn't have sex. Did we?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Oh, of course not, we didn't! You'd have known.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;But how and why?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Oh, that happens sometimes, that's divine essence and passion for you! I'm very happy about that. Many people don't care about me, they just want victory and stuff without having to work hard for it, that makes a fruitful training session all the more sweet. Anyway, gotta go, take good care of her, I trust you.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;... but I'm single, I've never had a child-&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Don't worry, she's all human, you know better than me how to raise that! Godspeed! *demanifests*&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;Ooooohhkay. Thank you for... for your trust, divine Karoka. Okay. Hey, folks, tell me, does that kinda thing happen often when you pray to gods of battles or victory instead?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T08:33:46-07:00","id":1417640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368280#post1368280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's beneficial how What Fire Has Wrought reconciled this element with love marriages including same-sex relationships by making a point of how the Houses see some use in childless couples as people that can readily take on adoptees.<br /> <br /> That and, if they're willing to take on the stigma, the uses of neomah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, remembering disgruntled scions still are superhuman heroes that can devastate a household in a moment of irrationality if pressured enough, and accomodating them, is definitely healthy.<br /> <br /> And though unrelated, it also made me think of &quot;magical adopted child&quot; tales like Momotaro or cabbage patch babbies folklore and the possibility of those as some form of elemental (probably wood?) perhaps.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1368591#post1368591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many gods, demons, fae, etc. can exhibit the full diversity of sexual orientations and gender identities that humans also have. A lot of the time, we try to write these nonhuman entities as being &quot;people&quot; first and foremost, and having them partake of some of the human condition is often helpful in doing so.<br /> <br /> There probably are orientations and gender identities that some non-humans have that humans don't\u2014in fact, I've got some specific ideas in that regard for the Mountain Folk\u2014but it's hard to find a good place to discuss that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now i'm quite curious indeed, as the jadeborn are that one race for whom gender has <b><i>no relation or role whatsoever with reproduction</i></b>, that is somewhere between reincarnation, mining or sculpting the ideal materials, depending on what aspects of their dogma each individual's focuses, i guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1369860#post1369860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a character I've made and still waiting for a chance to play, Marjan, who's a Dawn Caste, and, more relevant, a daughter and priestess of the (male) god of sparring/martial training.<br /> She was otherwise raised by a (single) mortal man.<br /> I've tried to make the circumstances of her birth sound properly mythological; her parents had no actual romantic or sexual interest in each other, her human father just prayed to the god for combat training in order to prepare for future bandit raids on the village (one could go for more straightforward, easier worship of gods of battles/victory, but those tends to be very in demand by everyone and not necessarily available or willing to answer, and sparring/training offers the added bonus of personal growth). In response, the god manifested directly, and started a very long and intensive training session that his worshiper nonetheless managed to power through; this session was so intense and filled with passion that its conclusion resulted in the manifestation of a newborn human girl, who, besides a knack for varied forms of combat as she grew up and the circumstances of her birth, was completely normal.<br /> <br /> This is the objective, serious pitch.<br /> <br /> But after reading this thread, I can't help but ruin the mythical feel by picturing the scene went more like this:<br /> Man: &quot;Thank you so much, o divine Karoka, I have grown immensely as an individual and protector of my community thanks to you and will be able to teach my peers how to-- wait, is that a baby?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;No need to thank me, that's my domain! And yes, that's our baby.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;Our baby? Ours?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Congratulations! You are the worthy co-progenitor of my spawn! Phew, I haven't had such a great sparring session in a while.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;But... but. We didn't have sex. Did we?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Oh, of course not, we didn't! You'd have known.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;But how and why?&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Oh, that happens sometimes, that's divine essence and passion for you! I'm very happy about that. Many people don't care about me, they just want victory and stuff without having to work hard for it, that makes a fruitful training session all the more sweet. Anyway, gotta go, take good care of her, I trust you.&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;... but I'm single, I've never had a child-&quot;<br /> God: &quot;Don't worry, she's all human, you know better than me how to raise that! Godspeed! *demanifests*&quot;<br /> Man: &quot;Ooooohhkay. Thank you for... for your trust, divine Karoka. Okay. Hey, folks, tell me, does that kinda thing happen often when you pray to gods of battles or victory instead?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds quite mythical to me, to be fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-11-2020, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T18:00:21-07:00","id":1417735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual?p=1369860#post1369860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a character I've made and still waiting for a chance to play, Marjan, who's a Dawn Caste, and, more relevant, a daughter and priestess of the (male) god of sparring/martial training.<br /> She was otherwise raised by a (single) mortal man.<br /> I've tried to make the circumstances of her birth sound properly mythological; her parents had no actual romantic or sexual interest in each other, her human father just prayed to the god for combat training in order to prepare for future bandit raids on the village (one could go for more straightforward, easier worship of gods of battles/victory, but those tends to be very in demand by everyone and not necessarily available or willing to answer, and sparring/training offers the added bonus of personal growth). In response, the god manifested directly, and started a very long and intensive training session that his worshiper nonetheless managed to power through; this session was so intense and filled with passion that its conclusion resulted in the manifestation of a newborn human girl, who, besides a knack for varied forms of combat as she grew up and the circumstances of her birth, was completely normal.<br /> <br /> This is the objective, serious pitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't pay close attention to this thread at the time, but I'm glad it was necromanced, because I love this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T21:32:08-07:00","id":1417767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1368060-hi-is-this-game-100-straight-and-fully-heterosexual#post1368060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my question is whether most non-human in Exalted possesses the same sexual orientation and gender identities as humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>So re: gender identities, I do remember one thing in 2e from one of the Ink Monkey Magnus bits: It's noted that other Primordials may have souls that exist outside the gender binary, but Kimbery exclusively does not.<br /> <br /> Obviously, that was years ago and in different hands, but there is some sort of foundation for non-binary spiritual beings out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 10-12-2020, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}